EO:10987,FRDOC:2025-06904,2025-06904,Proposed Rule,2025-04-23,90 FR 17182,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2025/04/23/2025-06904.txt,c73e1ec148adeb2f19e9d6d253e43d78b6c5e54545a8e398439c21f13cd30595,"In 1962 President Kennedy's Executive Order 10987 required agencies to create internal procedures for non-veterans to appeal adverse actions.\42\ President Richard Nixon's Executive Orders 11491 and 11787 transferred these internal appeals to the CSC, aligning the process for veterans and non- veterans.\43\ The Supreme Court also dramatically changed the legal landscape in Arnett v."
