EO:10988,FRDOC:2023-19806,2023-19806,Proposed Rule,2023-09-18,88 FR 63862,extension,modifying,True,False,False,,2,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2023/09/18/2023-19806.txt,b660a13345bf358b12bdcc0db43b3f3118bd64dd347a957ecfe0370a93de756b,"In short, the Veterans' Preference Act provided eligible veterans with adverse action protections and access to an appeals process.\29\ Then, in 1962, President John F. Kennedy issued Executive Order 10988 to extend adverse action rights to the broader civil service.\30\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
EO:10988,FRDOC:2024-06815,2024-06815,Rule,2024-04-09,89 FR 24982,extension,modifying,True,False,False,,2,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2024/04/09/2024-06815.txt,085737f4045ff2958a3cb739e6069fc244f94afe3cb10bb37f87ddcf0b662462,"In short, the Veterans' Preference Act provided eligible veterans with adverse action protections and access to an appeals process.\41\ Then, in 1962, President John F. Kennedy issued Executive Order 10988 to extend similar adverse action rights to a broader swath of the civil service, specifically, employees in the competitive service.\42\ ---------------------------------------------------------"
EO:10988,FRDOC:94-23395,94-23395,Uncategorized Document,1994-09-23,,revocation,ending,True,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1994/09/23/94-23395.txt,4e7c329966687629082e7aa59b1fe6e07a6a6a40b9f50c35710197eef90140f7,"The definition of ``Federal employee organization'' is in conformance with the definition of ``Federal employee organization'' in Executive Order 10988, January 17, 1962 which was revoked by Executive Order 11491 and reflects that this term refers to nonprofit associations or organizations which are composed of Federal employees."
