EO:13895,FRDOC:2022-16463,2022-16463,Proposed Rule,2022-08-01,87 FR 46918,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2022/08/01/2022-16463.txt,e1750e5374ecbd7a31a3431ac1869af2a491d2f9e06d63fd0ab9b5a849931363,"\1\ CMS defines ``underserved communities'' as ``populations sharing a particular characteristic, as well as geographic communities, that have been systematically denied a full opportunity to participate in aspects of economic, social, and civic life.'' CMS derives this definition from that of the same term in Executive Order 13895 (United States, Executive Office of the President [Joseph Biden]. "
