EO:9981,FRDOC:08-1468,08-1468,Presidential Document,2008-07-28,73 FR 43605,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2008/07/28/08-1468.txt,8bcd27daa8f12b6177a80bc7ec64ab5c7468332f6ae09d9fc7eea675326dc216,"On July 26, 1948, President Harry Truman signed Executive Order 9981, declaring ``that there shall be equality of treatment and opportunity for all persons in the armed services without regard to race, color, religion or national origin.'' Today, members of our Armed Forces come from many different backgrounds and cultures and are answering the call to service with bravery, decency, and resolve."
EO:9981,FRDOC:98-19040,98-19040,Presidential Document,1998-07-15,63 FR 38073,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,2,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1998/07/15/98-19040.txt,1ccd8937ab8303ea3a96ba85106af3dbda9dedffd9379d73bd491682af976dc3,"By signing Executive Order 9981, ``Establishing the President's Committee on Equality of Treatment and Opportunity in the Armed Services,'' he officially declared that ``there shall be equality of treatment and opportunity for all persons in the armed services without regard to race, color, religion or national origin.'' His action reflected the growing realization by more and more Americans that "
